-peak-range HIGH LOW]\n\nPreprocess FTIR spectra and calculate single-range or all-pairs cross-range\n2D-COS matrices.\n\noptions:\n  -h, --help            show this help message and exit\n  --config CONFIG       JSON wrapper or plain PipelineConfig file\n\ninput and output:\n  --input INPUT         wide CSV/TXT/TSV file, DPT file, or directory of DPT\n                        files\n  --output OUTPUT       output root (default: wrapper value, otherwise\n                        ./results)\n  --dpt-pattern DPT_PATTERN\n                        case-insensitive filename pattern for a DPT directory\n                        (default: *MIN.dpt)\n  --delimiter {auto,comma,tab,semicolon}\n                        wide-table delimiter (default: detect comma, tab, or\n                        semicolon)\n  --perturbation VALUE [VALUE ...]\n                        explicit perturbation values in input spectrum order\n\npipeline:\n  --range HIGH:LOW[:LABEL] [HIGH:LOW[:LABEL] ...]\n                        inclusive range; repeat for batch analysis. Colon or\n                        comma compact syntax is preferred; legacy '--range\n                        HIGH LOW' remains supported. For negative compact\n                        values use '--range=-1:-5[:LABEL]'.\n  --intensity {absorbance,percent_transmittance,fraction_transmittance,unknown}\n                        input intensity unit; conversion is only done for an\n                        explicit transmittance unit\n  --perturbation-order {preserve_file_order,sort_by_perturbation}\n                        preserve acquisition/file order by default, or\n                        explicitly sort by perturbation\n  --convention {canonical,2dpy_compatible}\n                        2D-COS matrix orientation/sign convention\n  --contour-levels CONTOUR_LEVELS\n                        number of contour levels used for exported figures\n  --display-percentile DISPLAY_PERCENTILE\n                        symmetric display-only color percentile in (0, 100]\n\npeak response-order analysis:\n  --peak WAVENUMBER[:LABEL][@RANGE]\n                        peak position to order; repeat at least twice. RANGE\n                        is an optional 1-based analysis-range index required\n                        when intervals overlap (examples: 1650:amide-I,\n                        1650:amide-I@1, 1200@2).\n  --peak-match-tolerance CM-1\n                        maximum distance to the nearest sampled grid point\n                        (default: 1 cm^-1)\n  --sync-threshold VALUE\n                        absolute synchronous signal cutoff for an\n                        indeterminate pair (default: 0)\n  --async-threshold VALUE\n                        absolute asynchronous signal cutoff for an\n                        indeterminate pair (default: 0)\n  --peak-relative-threshold FRACTION\n                        matrix-relative numerical signal cutoff; the effective\n                        cutoff is the larger of this fraction (0..1) times\n                        matrix max-abs and the absolute cutoff (default: 1e-6)\n  --analysis-order-note ANALYSIS_ORDER_NOTE\n                        optional context appended to the automatically derived\n                        perturbation-order facts; it cannot override the\n                        stored sequence\n\nbaseline correction:\n  --baseline {none,offset,constant,anchor_polynomial,anchor,asls,rubberband}\n                        baseline method\n  --offset-mode {minimum,window_median}\n                        constant/offset estimator\n  --offset-window HIGH LOW\n                        wavenumber interval used by offset window_median mode\n  --anchor-range HIGH LOW\n                        anchor interval; repeat this option to supply multiple\n                        intervals\n  --polynomial-order {0,1,2,3}\n                        anchor-polynomial order\n  --asls-lam ASLS_LAM   AsLS smoothness lambda\n  --asls-p ASLS_P       AsLS asymmetry in (0, 1)\n  --asls-diff-order ASLS_DIFF_ORDER\n                        AsLS finite-difference order\n  --asls-max-iter ASLS_MAX_ITER\n                        AsLS maximum iterations\n  --asls-tol ASLS_TOL   AsLS convergence tolerance\n  --rubberband-segments SEGMENT [SEGMENT ...]\n                        segment count (one value) or explicit segment boundary\n                        indices\n  --rubberband-lam RUBBERBAND_LAM\n                        optional rubberband smoothing lambda\n  --rubberband-diff-order RUBBERBAND_DIFF_ORDER\n                        rubberband smoothing finite-difference order\n  --rubberband-smooth-half-window RUBBERBAND_SMOOTH_HALF_WINDOW\n                        optional rubberband pre-smoothing half-window\n\noptional Savitzky-Golay smoothing:\n  --smooth              enable smoothing (disabled by default)\n  --no-smooth           explicitly disable smoothing\n  --smoothing-window SMOOTHING_WINDOW\n                        Savitzky-Golay window length\n  --smoothing-polyorder SMOOTHING_POLYORDER\n                        Savitzky-Golay polynomial order\n  --smoothing-mode {interp,mirror,constant,nearest,wrap}\n                        Savitzky-Golay edge mode\n\noptional normalization:\n  --normalization {none,vector,reference_peak}\n                        spectrum-wise normalization method (none by default)\n  --reference-peak-range HIGH LOW\n                        reference interval required by reference_peak\n                        normalization\n\nConfiguration precedence: explicit CLI options override JSON values. Ranges\nuse: repeated --range, then wrapper JSON ranges, then legacy pipeline low/high\nfields. A plain PipelineConfig JSON still requires --input. Wrapper-relative\npaths are resolved from the JSON file directory.\n",
